# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The full-match ground truth and licensed match assets are not public.
#
# Everything below either is a private asset, would leak the answer, or is generated output. The
# Ignore rules do not remove tracked files or erase Git history. Review both before publication.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# -- private ground truth ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ground truth files remain local, including the organizer's public correctness sample.
evaluation/gt/
*_possession_gt.csv
*_possession_gt_meta.json
*_possession_gt_reference.csv
possession_by_frame.pkl

# -- submissions -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Any file in results/ is a set of labels for the whole match. A perfect one is a copy of the
# ground truth, so the folder ships empty and stays that way.
evaluation/results/*.csv
evaluation/results/README.md

# ...with one deliberate exception. The baselines are computed from the ATD alone -- the same ATD
# every enrolled participant has -- and never read a ground truth of any kind, so they carry no
# information about the answer. They ship so that a fresh clone has something real to score.
!evaluation/results/baseline_*.csv
evaluation/reports/
evaluation/scoreboard.csv

# -- gated data --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/ is committed empty, with only its .gitkeep marker, so the folder participants are told to unpack
# into actually exists in a fresh clone. Everything they put in it stays out of git.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep

*.mp4
*.gzip
*.pl3container

# -- internal documents ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The upstream challenge overview and README are preserved under official_documentation/.
# The root README is the project-specific research overview and links to that archive.
#
# *.pdf stays as insurance: internal decks and proposals have a habit of landing in the working
# tree, and this repository is public.
*.pdf

# Keep local organiser tooling out of the repository.
organizers/

# -- editors and build artifacts ---------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
.DS_Store

.venv-mlops/
.venv*/

# Local operating notes and agent instructions
docs/
setup/
AGENTS.md
AGENTS_NEURAL_ADDENDUM.md
CLAUDE.md
.agents/
.claude/

# Local experiment metadata and development caches
artifacts/
mlruns/
.mlflow/
mlruns.db
mlruns.db-*
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Local secrets, scratch notes, and editor/experiment backups
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.remember/
# Local research scratch summary; the public overview is in README.md.
/summary.md
*.bak
*.tmp
*.pt
*.pth
# The reviewed N018 checkpoint is explicitly approved for competition release.
!models/n018/best.pt
*.safetensors
*.npy
*.npz
*.parquet
*.pkl
